From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 04:48:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08040/11362] The same depth mislabel lived in the planner the
 gate guards, and four claims were stronger than what was measured

PHASE 3 (previously uncommitted while PHASE 4 sat on top of it) plus the response
to the adversarial review of Phases 1-4. All 15 findings applied; none were wrong.

THE CODE CHANGE. Phase 3 split `goal_unreached_within_depth` out of
`queue_exhausted` in `_goal_satisfiability_check`. The review found the identical
conflation still live in `plan_in_model` -- the planner that gate exists to guard --
and Phase 3's own evidence file was the proof: `tn36_depth_label.json` records
`plan_at_max_depth_40.diagnostics.termination_reason == "queue_exhausted"` on a goal
the same triple plans at depth 61 with the cap lifted. `termination_reason` is now
three-way (budget, then depth, then exhaustion) with `depth_truncated_nodes` on every
exit that ran a search.

Inertness is MEASURED: the git-HEAD module is loaded into a separate namespace and
both versions run 600 randomised cases across four engine families and both search
loops -- 0 return-value differences, with 146 genuine relabels and 111 preserved
`queue_exhausted` verdicts proving it is a split and not a rename. 9 tests, 6/6 real
mutations killed, inert control survives.

FOUR CLAIMS RESTATED (originals preserved; never-prune):
- Phase 2's "games REACHING a non-degenerate engine 1/5 -> 3/5" is PARSE-LEVEL and
  offline, not funnel. Restated as attempts producing parseable, non-inert code; the
  live funnel is unchanged at 1 of 6, and "reaching" is reserved for policy reach.
- That count includes tu93, which the same requirement calls junk. On the artifact's
  own strong bar the net new game is sc25 alone, n=1, p=1.000.
- Phase 1's `cell_recall 0.9474` engine gets 0 of 6 transitions fully right.
- The change gate is downgraded QUALIFIED YES -> NO for mask-off. exp6011 and exp6013
  do not disagree: both reject the known-good dc22 control mask-off 3/3 on the whole
  corpus, and exp6013 states it as a finding. Also surfaced: tn36-on, the sole
  must-not-fire point, passes with n_noop=0, so one of three sub-conditions was never
  exercised.

The orphan guard was giving a false clean bill on `arc_engine_static_validation` --
it matches none of the lint's solver shapes. `_is_solver_like` now sees the
induce-path gating surface and the module is allow-listed with its reason, pinned by
a test that fails if the entry is removed.

Nothing shipped changed behaviour: no threshold moved, no flag flipped, MAX_ACTIONS
and the early-stop grace untouched. 13 stale registered artifacts discharged through
the sanctioned freshness_acknowledgements path with hash + reason + evidence; every
artifact diff is additive. 8 tracked historical artifacts carrying test-suite
timestamp rewrites were content-diffed and reverted.

